trol; DM, diabetes mellitus; NA, not applicable; OR, odds ratio; SC-Hosp, serum creatinine during hospitalization.</p></fn><fn id="t8-fn2"><p>For each model, the predictor variables used in the AKI sample were entered in a single step in the CON sample.</p></fn><fn id="t8-fn3"><p>Model 1 Likelihood ratio <italic>&#x003c7;</italic><sup>2</sup> (LRC)=1219.8, d.f.=7, <italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.0001; Somer's <italic>D</italic>=0.62, <italic>c</italic>=0.81.</p></fn><fn id="t8-fn4"><p>Model 2 LRC=1470.2, d.f.=4, <italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.0001; Somer's <italic>D</italic>=0.63, <italic>c</italic>=0.81.</p></fn><fn id="t8-fn5"><p>Model 3 LRC=10810.0, d.f.=6, <italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.0001; Somer's <italic>D</italic>=0.64, <italic>c</italic>=0.82.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>